+\paragraph{Bridge status vocabulary}
+The core TRL specification and the ResearchLedger v2.2 bridge are separate layers with different native status names. Core TRL derives claim labels \texttt{unsupported}, \texttt{supported}, \texttt{verified}, \texttt{contested} and \texttt{stale}. ResearchLedger v2.2 derives \texttt{hypothesis}, \texttt{provisional}, \texttt{supported}, \texttt{mixed}, \texttt{contradicted} and \texttt{withdrawn}. The historical tracked-proxy study reports the latter labels because it executes the ResearchLedger bridge directly. In that bridge, \texttt{hypothesis} is returned when no currently sufficient live support path has positive support level; \texttt{provisional} corresponds to a live path with observed/checked evidence; and \texttt{supported} corresponds to a live path whose members are verified. The reported \texttt{supported}$\to$\texttt{hypothesis}$\to$\texttt{supported} lifecycle therefore demonstrates loss and restoration of bridge support, not a transition in the core TRL state table. Keeping the vocabularies explicit avoids treating two independently evolved implementation labels as identical constructs.
